From 344c0bea3e03e252bb4ce4a4521b1862e7e2942d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Techma2004 <techma@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 06:56:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Redesign login page and portal for a professional, enterprise
 look
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Add icons.js: a small inline-SVG icon set (stroke, currentColor) to
  replace every emoji glyph used in the login/portal UI (toast icons,
  sidebar nav, dashboard stat cards, modal close, mobile nav toggle,
  sign-out button, password show/hide, print button, AI import
  dropzone). No icon library dependency, no network fetch — keeps the
  offline-first footprint of the app.
- Refine design tokens in styles.css: calmer navy/brass palette,
  tighter border-radius and shadows, a proper system font stack (no
  external font CDN), toned-down font weights/sizes across buttons,
  badges, sidebar, dashboard cards and the portal-wide component
  system. Also adds a matching '.toast.warning' style and a
  currentColor-based icon treatment throughout.
- Rebuild login.html: single-accent brand panel (no decorative rings
  or oversized circular crest), icon-based password visibility
  toggle, tightened responsive breakpoints.
- Rebuild the portal shell (portal.html/portal.js): compact sidebar
  with real icons per section, cleaner topbar, icon-driven stat cards
  and workflow call-outs, refreshed modal/toast chrome. All content
  is still rendered from the live API responses in state — no mock
  or placeholder data was introduced.
- Fixed a real mobile-cascade bug introduced by the redesign: the
  navbar's height shrinks to 64px under 650px width, but login.html's
  own inline styles for .login-page were unconditional and always
  applied the 72px desktop offset, leaving a visible gap under the
  navbar on phones. Added the matching mobile override so the two
  stay in sync.
- Cleaned up now-dead/conflicting mobile CSS left over from the old
  emoji-based stat icons and the old circular login crest image.
